Task 3: Test VM Network Connectivity Across Multiple Hosts
Subtask 3.1: Start and Configure Test VMs
Power On Virtual Machines

Start all three test VMs:

test-vm-network-17
test-vm-network-17-host1
test-vm-network-17-host2
Configure IP Addresses

Connect to each VM console and configure static IP addresses:

VM 1 (test-vm-network-17):

# Connect via console
nmcli con add type ethernet con-name lab-net ifname eth0
nmcli con mod lab-net ipv4.addresses 192.168.100.101/24
nmcli con mod lab-net ipv4.method manual
nmcli con up lab-net
VM 2 (test-vm-network-17-host1):

nmcli con add type ethernet con-name lab-net ifname eth0
nmcli con mod lab-net ipv4.addresses 192.168.100.102/24
nmcli con mod lab-net ipv4.method manual
nmcli con up lab-net
VM 3 (test-vm-network-17-host2):

nmcli con add type ethernet con-name lab-net ifname eth0
nmcli con mod lab-net ipv4.addresses 192.168.100.103/24
nmcli con mod lab-net ipv4.method manual
nmcli con up lab-net
Subtask 3.2: Test Basic Network Connectivity
Ping Test Between VMs

From VM 1, test connectivity to other VMs:

# Test connectivity to VM on same host
ping -c 4 192.168.100.102

# Test connectivity to VM on different host
ping -c 4 192.168.100.103
Verify Network Interface Configuration

On each VM, verify network configuration:

# Check IP configuration
ip addr show eth0

# Check routing table
ip route show

# Verify MAC address assignment
ip link show eth0
Test Network Performance

Install and use network testing tools:

# Install network tools
dnf install -y iperf3 traceroute

# On VM 1 (server)
iperf3 -s

# On VM 2 (client)
iperf3 -c 192.168.100.101 -t 10
Subtask 3.3: Advanced Network Testing
Test Cross-Host Communication

Verify that VMs on different hosts can communicate:

# From VM on Host 1 to VM on Host 2
traceroute 192.168.100.103

# Check network latency
ping -c 10 192.168.100.103 | tail -1
Monitor Network Traffic

Use network monitoring tools to observe traffic:

# Install monitoring tools
dnf install -y tcpdump netstat-nat

# Monitor network interface
tcpdump -i eth0 -n icmp

# Check network statistics
netstat -i
Test Network Failover

Simulate network issues and test connectivity:

# Temporarily disable network interface
nmcli con down lab-net

# Test connectivity (should fail)
ping 192.168.100.102

# Re-enable interface
nmcli con up lab-net

# Verify connectivity restored
ping 192.168.100.102
