Troubleshooting Common Issues
Network Connectivity Problems
Issue: VMs cannot communicate across hosts

Solution:

# Check host network configuration
ip addr show
ip route show

# Verify VLAN configuration
cat /proc/net/vlan/config

# Check firewall rules
firewall-cmd --list-all
MAC Address Pool Issues
Issue: MAC address conflicts or assignment failures

Solution:

# Check MAC pool usage in RHVM
# Navigate to Administration → Configure → MAC Address Pools
# Verify pool ranges and usage statistics

# Reset VM network interface if needed
virsh domif-setlink test-vm-network-17 vnet0 down
virsh domif-setlink test-vm-network-17 vnet0 up
VLAN Configuration Problems
Issue: VLAN traffic not passing between hosts

Solution:

# Verify VLAN interface creation
ip link show | grep 100

# Check switch configuration (if applicable)
# Ensure VLAN 100 is configured on physical switches

# Test VLAN connectivity at host level
ping -I eth1.100 192.168.100.11
Conclusion
In this lab, you have successfully accomplished several critical networking tasks in a virtualized environment:

Key Achievements:

Logical Network Configuration: You created and configured a custom logical network (lab-network-17) with VLAN tagging, enabling network segmentation and isolation for virtual machines.

MAC Address Pool Management: You established a custom MAC address pool to ensure consistent and organized MAC address assignment for VM network interfaces, preventing conflicts and enabling better network management.

Cross-Host Network Testing: You verified that virtual machines can communicate effectively across different virtualization hosts, demonstrating the power and flexibility of virtualized networking.

Why This Matters:

Enterprise Readiness: These skills are essential for managing production virtualization environments where network isolation, performance, and reliability are critical.

Scalability: Understanding logical networks and MAC pools enables you to design and implement large-scale virtualized infrastructures that can grow with organizational needs.

Troubleshooting Foundation: The testing and verification procedures you learned provide the foundation for diagnosing and resolving network issues in complex virtualized environments.

Certification Preparation: This hands-on experience directly supports your preparation for the Red Hat Certified Specialist in Virtualization exam, demonstrating practical competency in virtualized networking.

The networking concepts and procedures you've mastered in this lab form the backbone of modern data center operations, cloud computing platforms, and enterprise virtualization deployments. These skills will serve you well as you advance in your virtualization and cloud infrastructure career.
